## 2. Dhaka to Toronto Flight Biman Bangladesh Airlines

Biman Bangladesh Airlines is an important option for passengers travelling between Bangladesh and Canada.

The airline operates its Toronto service using Boeing 787-9 Dreamliner aircraft. Its scheduled Toronto route includes a technical stop in Rome, Italy.

This means passengers should distinguish between a nonstop flight and a flight operated under one flight number with an intermediate stop.

### Biman Bangladesh Flight Route

The scheduled route is:

- Departure: Dhaka (DAC)
- Technical stop: Rome Fiumicino (FCO)
- Arrival: Toronto Pearson (YYZ)

The flight operates as Biman flight BG305 on the outbound journey, with BG306 serving the return direction.

The technical stop and operating arrangements may change, so check the latest itinerary when purchasing your ticket.

### Biman Bangladesh Flight Schedule

Biman's published Northern Summer 2026 routing information lists three weekly services on Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday.

The schedule can change between airline seasons, and actual departure times may vary.

Before travelling, confirm:

- Your departure date and local departure time.
- The Rome stop duration.
- Whether you remain on the same aircraft.
- Your Toronto arrival time.
- Any changes to the return schedule.

You can check available flights directly through the official Biman website:

https://www.biman-airlines.com/

### Why Consider Biman Bangladesh Airlines?

Some passengers prefer Biman because it offers a Bangladesh-based airline option for the Dhaka–Toronto journey.

Potential advantages include:

- Departure from Dhaka.
- A familiar airline for many Bangladeshi passengers.
- Boeing 787-9 Dreamliner aircraft on the scheduled route.
- Economy, Premium Economy and Business Class options, subject to availability.
- An itinerary that does not necessarily require changing aircraft at the technical stop.

